Package: RUMBLE
Type: Package
Title: Reproducible Understanding of Microbiome Biomarkers with Leakage-free Explainability
Version: 3.2.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Lucas", "Fett", email = "lucas.fett2021@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0006-0596-3991"))
Description: RUMBLE (Reproducible Understanding of Microbiome Biomarkers with
    Leakage-free Explainability)
    implements a publication-quality consensus machine learning framework for
    identifying microbial biomarkers from high-throughput sequencing data.
    The package integrates multiple classification algorithms (Random Forest,
    XGBoost, Elastic Net, KNN) via the tidymodels ecosystem with nested
    cross-validation, and provides model-agnostic interpretability through
    SHAP values and permutation importance (via DALEX). It handles
    compositional microbiome data using centered log-ratio (CLR)
    transformations with strict anti-leakage safeguards. Version 3.1
    introduces inter-fold stability assessment, feature selection frequency
    analysis, SHAP overfitting diagnostics, hyperparameter stability
    reporting, cost-sensitive learning for class imbalance, Spearman-based
    directional metrics, and pooled out-of-fold ROC curves. Descriptive
    direction metrics replace statistically invalid p-values on SHAP
    correlations. Differential abundance integration with ANCOM-BC, ALDEx2,
    and Wilcoxon methods enables rigorous multi-evidence validation of
    biomarker candidates.
